Licensing for the base-seven Heraclitus transform release
=======================================================

Copyright (c) 2026 Roger Gujord, to the extent copyright subsists.

The public distribution uses different licenses for different components:

* Python and Lean source code, build/verification scripts, and workflow
  configuration: MIT. Full text: LICENSES/MIT.txt.
* Manuscript (PDF, LaTeX and text), documentation, bibliography, certificate
  JSON, discovery inputs, authored reports and metadata: Creative Commons
  Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
  Full text: LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt.

These licenses apply by component, not as a choice between two licenses for
the same file. Source code quoted within prose remains MIT. Mathematical
facts are not restricted by this notice. Third-party names, citations and
license texts retain their existing status; no rights in third-party works
are asserted. The compiler and standard library are not bundled here and
retain their own licenses.

Private development archives (archive/) are excluded from the public
distribution and from this license grant. They are retained unchanged for
historical provenance. This notice grants no additional rights in them.

The manuscript, programs and formalization were developed using OpenAI
Codex under Roger Gujord's direction. See docs/provenance.md for the roles,
executed checks and limitations. Licensing does not certify mathematical
correctness, independent review, novelty or authorship of every expression.

Suggested attribution: Roger Gujord, The base-seven Heraclitus transform:
manuscript and reproducible proof package, version 1.0.0,
DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23912682.
